00:57:54,345 --> 00:57:55,805
You know how much

795
00:57:56,598 --> 00:57:59,058
I wanted to play a concerto with you, so
why?

796
00:58:00,351 --> 00:58:01,186
Why…

797
00:58:03,229 --> 00:58:05,565
Why did you choose Choi Jeong-yo
instead of me?

798
00:58:05,648 --> 00:58:07,775
Do I really have to spell it out to you?

799
00:58:08,276 --> 00:58:11,070
At the Noblesse Concert you said that I
was good!

800
00:58:11,154 --> 00:58:12,280
You said…

801
00:58:13,281 --> 00:58:15,783
you said you'd come watch me perform
next time!

802
00:58:15,867 --> 00:58:17,452
Your performance at Noblesse…

803
00:58:18,536 --> 00:58:20,497
it wasn't good because you played well.

804
00:58:21,581 --> 00:58:24,125
It was Choi Jeong-yo who led that
performance,

805
00:58:25,376 --> 00:58:28,046
and you were just riding the wave of his
raw emotion.

806
00:58:29,088 --> 00:58:31,716
You and Choi Jeong-yo are fundamentally
different.

807
00:58:31,799 --> 00:58:34,677
You're calculating, but he acts
on instinct.

808
00:58:35,845 --> 00:58:37,514
You analyze the structure,

809
00:58:38,014 --> 00:58:41,726
while he pours music straight from
his heart, like erupting lava.

810
00:58:42,435 --> 00:58:46,105
And that's why people think your music is
perfect but an absolute bore to

811
00:58:46,189 --> 00:58:47,398
listen to.

812
00:58:48,483 --> 00:58:49,651
But when they hear his,

813
00:58:50,193 --> 00:58:52,946
they're completely mesmerized, even if
it's imperfect.

814
00:58:53,029 --> 00:58:54,155
And that's…

815
00:58:55,490 --> 00:58:57,325
That's not something that can just be
taught!

816
00:58:57,408 --> 00:59:00,119
CM No, that's not true at all!

817
00:59:00,828 --> 00:59:01,996
You're wrong, Mr. Kang.

818
00:59:03,331 --> 00:59:04,457
You don't know that,

819
00:59:05,416 --> 00:59:06,751
it was Pi-o who led me that day.

820
00:59:06,834 --> 00:59:09,837
I was able to play the piano because
of him, and he's the one who evoked

821
00:59:09,921 --> 00:59:11,005
those emotions in me!

822
00:59:11,089 --> 00:59:14,717
Why do you compare us like that when you
don't even know the full story?

823
00:59:15,510 --> 00:59:17,887
- You can stop now.
- What do you mean, stop?

824
00:59:17,971 --> 00:59:19,430
I'm telling the truth.

825
00:59:19,931 --> 00:59:22,934
That you're much better than me and a
generational talent!

826
00:59:23,601 --> 00:59:26,229
I find your friendship oddly intriguing,
but…

827
00:59:28,856 --> 00:59:29,691
Pi-o,

828
00:59:31,693 --> 00:59:33,069
do you see what I mean now?

829
00:59:34,445 --> 00:59:38,700
You know who will be the one to end up
utterly broken between the two of you.

830
00:59:47,250 --> 00:59:49,252
- CM
- CM

831
00:59:49,794 --> 00:59:50,628
Pi-o.

832
01:00:12,900 --> 01:00:13,818
Wait, Pi-o…

833
01:00:15,820 --> 01:00:17,280
Can't you leave my son alone?

834
01:00:19,449 --> 01:00:20,491
I'm so sorry I just--

835
01:00:20,575 --> 01:00:21,909
Do you still not get it?

836
01:00:22,994 --> 01:00:24,329
All of this is your fault.

837
01:00:24,871 --> 01:00:25,788
I'm warning you.

838
01:00:26,581 --> 01:00:27,957
Don't talk to Pi-o ever again.

839
01:00:28,041 --> 01:00:29,626
And if I ever find out you did,

840
01:00:31,252 --> 01:00:33,504
I'll make sure you regret it. You got
that?

841
01:00:40,053 --> 01:00:40,887
CM

842
01:01:04,369 --> 01:01:05,203
Pi-o?

843
01:01:09,499 --> 01:01:10,333
Pi-o.

844
01:01:15,296 --> 01:01:16,130
N

845
01:01:17,048 --> 01:01:17,882
Pi-o.

846
01:01:23,805 --> 01:01:24,639
Pi-o!

847
01:01:36,025 --> 01:01:37,402
Pi-o! Pi-o!

848
01:01:38,152 --> 01:01:39,195
Pi-o, wake up!

849
01:01:40,071 --> 01:01:40,905
Kang Pi-o!

850
01:01:41,781 --> 01:01:42,615
Pi-o!

851
01:01:43,741 --> 01:01:46,619
SPECIAL THANKS TO SUNWOO YE-KWON
FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

852
01:02:07,557 --> 01:02:09,559
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

853
01:02:10,059 --> 01:02:11,894
Why do you say I'll never make it?

854
01:02:12,395 --> 01:02:14,272
Because you have no talent.

855
01:02:14,897 --> 01:02:17,859
I'm not a genius. If I can't even get
recognition from competitions, who would

856
01:02:17,942 --> 01:02:19,527
ever bother listening to me play?

857
01:02:19,610 --> 01:02:22,321
I want you to enter the same competition
I'm entering.

858
01:02:23,406 --> 01:02:25,408
Since when has your pinky been like this?

859
01:02:25,491 --> 01:02:27,702
Of all pieces, why did he make
us play the same one?

860
01:02:27,785 --> 01:02:30,830
You're not in a good place right now.
Cut it out! Stop, stop!

861
01:02:30,913 --> 01:02:33,624
Do you want to get kicked out before
you even get to compete?

862
01:02:33,708 --> 01:02:35,001
If I don't win that competition,

863
01:02:35,084 --> 01:02:37,211
I'm going to quit playing the piano.
